Subject: if_bridge: learn multicast-router ports from IGMP queries

---
 share/man/man4/bridge.4         |  10 +
 sys/net/if_bridge.c             | 316 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 tests/sys/net/if_bridge_test.sh | 181 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 446 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)

diff --git a/share/man/man4/bridge.4 b/share/man/man4/bridge.4
index b103e61c8..dab98f1e8 100644
--- a/share/man/man4/bridge.4
+++ b/share/man/man4/bridge.4
@@ -614,6 +614,13 @@ forwarding to only those ports.
 This is disabled by default; forwarding falls back to flooding whenever no
 listener state is known, for non-IP multicast, and for exempt link-local
 control traffic.
+.Pp
+Member ports on which IGMP membership queries are seen are additionally
+learned as multicast-router ports.
+A learned group is forwarded to its listener ports and to any router port on
+the same VLAN, so that pruning does not blackhole multicast that a router
+needs to relay.
+Router ports are aged like listener state and are refreshed by each query.
 The following
 .Xr sysctl 8
 variables control and observe this behavior:
@@ -643,6 +650,9 @@ the snooping parser.
 .It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_expired
 Read-only count of MDB listener entries removed because their membership aged
 out.
+.It Va net.link.bridge.mdb_routers
+Read-only count of multicast-router ports currently learned from IGMP
+membership queries.
 .El
 .Pp
 Writing any value to one of the read-only counters resets it to zero.
